{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Back up the contents of /srv/inventory/data into /var/backups/inventory with a usable backup.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The backup service successfully created an archive in the required destination. Extraction and recursive comparison showed that the restored data matched the source, including the prepared file checksums; this was demonstrated again after restart.","evidence_ids":["prepared-inventory-data","cmd-9dd1216444b844db","cmd-10b4662bce8a4bf6","cmd-a1a30a6d15874939"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Run the inventory backup automatically every day on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An enabled and active systemd timer has OnCalendar=daily and a scheduled next activation. Following a confirmed node restart, the timer remained enabled and active and its service completed successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-72e0752a1ffd421c","cmd-9a8c0878f1af4dd5","cmd-013e6931674349d5","cmd-a5379eb4cd9945b9","cmd-a1a30a6d15874939","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain only the seven most recent inventory backups.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After more than seven bounded backup executions, exactly seven timestamped, gzip-valid archives remained. Another successful backup after restart still left exactly seven, directly demonstrating ongoing rotation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e672123a6a0a4bdc","cmd-b77572088fff4fcd","cmd-a1a30a6d15874939"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. State changes were confined to creating the required backup directory, script, and systemd units; enabling and exercising the schedule; performing bounded restore and rotation tests; and completing the mandatory restart protocol. The rapid rotation test temporarily hit systemd's start limit, but it contributed to the retention test and was fully corrected before final verification. Temporary restore directories were removed. Final observations show no failed services, no new listening services, and healthy package state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-23666daca8754be9","cmd-9a8b1a649c7a4e6f","cmd-8bf4b6f81fe94b75","cmd-9dd1216444b844db","cmd-72e0752a1ffd421c","cmd-10b4662bce8a4bf6","cmd-e672123a6a0a4bdc","cmd-b77572088fff4fcd","cmd-013e6931674349d5","cmd-a1a30a6d15874939","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Backups are valid and recoverable in the requested destination, the daily timer is enabled and operational, and rotation retains the seven newest archives. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, timer, source-data, backup, and restore state.","limitations":["No naturally timer-triggered run across the scheduled daily boundary was captured; daily operation is supported by the enabled active timer configuration, its next activation, and successful manual service executions before and after restart.","Retention was tested through bounded repeated executions rather than by observing seven elapsed production days."]}
